  "id": "Compound::DB06144 - Gene::3358",
  "verbalization": "Sertindole appears to interact with Htr2c through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Sertindole binds to Htr1e, which then participates in serotonin receptor activity, ultimately leading to Htr2c being involved in this process. This implies that Sertindole may modulate Htr2c through the activation of serotonin receptors, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways. The consistent binding to Htr1e across multiple paths supports a central role for this receptor in mediating the interaction between Sertindole and Htr2c. The observed relationships highlight a potential mechanism by which Sertindole could affect Htr2c, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
